@host = http://localhost:5068
@apiKey = local-dev-test-key-12345
@token = paste-the-token-field-from-the-login-response-here

### Health check (no auth)
GET {{host}}/health

### Login — validates against ProxyUsers, returns the shared X-API-Key + a personal JWT
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "Admin",
  "password": "AdminChrisAfflu"
}

### List proxy users (Admin role only — needs the JWT from login, not X-API-Key)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a proxy user (Admin role only)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "new-user",
  "password": "a-strong-password-123",
  "role": "Standard"
}

### View the audit log (any authenticated role — PIN/payload redacted for Standard)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/transactions?page=1&pageSize=25
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### KYC face verification — forwards to the real NIA upstream API
# Replace pinNumber with a real/sandbox Ghana Card PIN and image with a
# real Base64 PNG (640x480 min, under 1MB) before sending.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/selfie/verification/kyc/face
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pinNumber": "GHA-123456789-0",
  "image": "<base64-png>"
}

### YES/NO face verification — forwards to the real NIA upstream API
POST {{host}}/api/v1/selfie/verification/yes_no/face
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pinNumber": "GHA-123456789-0",
  "image": "<base64-png>"
}

### Generic proxy passthrough example
GET {{host}}/api/v1/proxy/some-upstream-path
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
